  "domain": "advanced-math",
  "skill": "equivalent-expressions",
  "title": "Factoring patterns to spot fast",
  "minutes": 6,
  "hook": "Common factor first, then look for a difference of squares, a perfect square or a simple trinomial.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "If $x^{2} - y^{2} = 36$ and $x - y = 4$, what is $x + y$?",
      "choices": [
        "9",
        "32",
        "40",
        "144"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$36 = (x + y)(x - y) = (x + y) \\times 4$, so $x + y = 9$.",
      "gate": true
    },
    {
      "type": "recall",
      "prompt": "From memory: factor $a^{2} - b^{2}$.",
      "answer": "$(a + b)(a - b)$: the difference of squares.",
      "skip_if": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Factor $x^{2} - 49$.",
      "choices": [
        "$(x - 7)(x + 7)$",
        "$(x - 7)^{2}$",
        "$(x - 49)(x + 1)$",
        "$x(x - 49)$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$49 = 7^{2}$, so it's a difference of squares.",
      "skip_if": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "prompt": "Factor $x^{2} + 5x + 6$.",
      "lines": [
        "Two numbers with product 6 and sum 5",
        "$(x + 2)(x +$ ___)"
      ],
      "accept": [
        "3"
      ],
      "why": "$2 \\times 3 = 6$ and $2 + 3 = 5$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Which equals $4x^{2} - 12x + 9$?",
      "choices": [
        "$(2x - 3)^{2}$",
        "$(2x + 3)^{2}$",
        "$(4x - 3)(x - 3)$",
        "$(2x - 9)(2x - 1)$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$(2x - 3)^{2} = 4x^{2} - 12x + 9$: a perfect square."
    },
    {
      "type": "build",
      "prompt": "Build the factored form of $x^{2} - 2x - 15$ from the tiles.",
      "tiles": [
        "$(x - 5)$",
        "$(x + 3)$",
        "$(x + 5)$",
        "$(x - 3)$",
        "$(x - 15)$",
        "$(x + 1)$"
      ],
      "answers": [
        [
          0,
          1
        ],
        [
          1,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "why": "Find two numbers that multiply to $-15$ and add to $-2$: $-5$ and 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "spot",
      "prompt": "Factoring $3x^{2} - 12$ completely. Tap the line with the mistake.",
      "lines": [
        "Take out the common factor: $3(x^{2} - 4)$",
        "Difference of squares: $3(x - 2)(x + 2)$",
        "So $3x^{2} - 12 = (3x - 6)(x - 2)$"
      ],
      "wrong": 2,
      "why": "$3(x - 2)(x + 2) = (3x - 6)(x + 2)$. The last factor should be $(x + 2)$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Factor $2x^{2} + 7x + 3$.",
      "choices": [
        "$(2x + 1)(x + 3)$",
        "$(2x + 3)(x + 1)$",
        "$(2x - 1)(x - 3)$",
        "$2(x + 3)(x + 1)$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$(2x + 1)(x + 3) = 2x^{2} + 6x + x + 3 = 2x^{2} + 7x + 3$."
    }
  ],
  "keys": [
    "Always take out the greatest common factor first.",
    "$a^{2} - b^{2} = (a + b)(a - b)$, and $a^{2} \\pm$ 2ab $+ b^{2} = (a \\pm b)^{2}$.",
    "For $x^{2} + bx + c$, find two numbers that multiply to $c$ and add to $b$."
  ],
  "recall": [
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Factor $x^{2} - 16$.",
      "choices": [
        "$(x - 4)(x + 4)$",
        "$(x - 4)^{2}$",
        "$(x - 8)(x + 2)$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$16 = 4^{2}$."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "prompt": "Factor $x^{2} - 7x + 10$.",
      "lines": [
        "Product 10, sum $-7$",
        "$(x - 2)(x -$ ___)"
      ],
      "accept": [
        "5"
      ],
      "why": "$-2 \\times -5 = 10$ and $-2 + -5 = -7$."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "$9x^{2} + 6x + 1$ equals:",
      "choices": [
        "$(3x + 1)^{2}$",
        "$(3x - 1)^{2}$",
        "$(9x + 1)(x + 1)$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$(3x)^{2} + 2(3x)(1) + 1^{2}$."
